meltify-ts — third-party notices
=================================

This project reimplements behaviour from ZenTenApp/meltify (the repository owner's work)
and uses the following third-party code and data.

1. bcrypt_pbkdf + Blowfish port
   File: src/core/crypto/bcrypt-pbkdf.ts
   Derived from the npm package "bcrypt-pbkdf" v1.0.2, itself a 1:1 port of
   OpenBSD blowfish.c and bcrypt_pbkdf.c. The only change is replacing its
   tweetnacl SHA-512 with @noble/hashes.
   - Blowfish: Copyright 1997 Niels Provos <provos@physnet.uni-hamburg.de>, BSD-3-Clause.
   - bcrypt_pbkdf: Copyright (c) 2013 Ted Unangst <tedu@openbsd.org>, ISC.
   - JavaScript performance work: Copyright 2016 Joyent Inc, author Alex Wilson, ISC.
   The full licence text is preserved in the file header.

2. Monero CryptoNote English word list
   File: src/core/derive/monero-wordlist.ts
   Source: monero-project/monero src/mnemonics/english.h (BSD-3-Clause), via
   github.com/chekist32/go-monero v0.2.5. The list is data, reproduced in its
   original order.

3. BIP39 English word list
   Provided by @scure/bip39 (MIT), originating from the Bitcoin BIPs repository.

4. Cryptographic and encoding libraries (MIT, audited, zero-dependency)
   - @noble/hashes  — SHA-2, SHA-3/Keccak, RIPEMD-160, BLAKE2, HMAC
   - @noble/curves  — Ed25519, secp256k1, BIP340 Schnorr
   - @noble/ciphers — AES-256-CTR
   - @scure/bip39   — BIP39 phrases and seeds
   - @scure/bip32   — BIP32 HD derivation
   - @scure/base    — base58/xmr/xrp, bech32/bech32m, base32, base64

5. Golden test vectors
   test/golden/goldens.ts — values copied from ZenTenApp/meltify
   internal/derive/golden.go (captured upstream from seedify v1.36.0).
